config OPLUS_HEALTHINFO
	tristate "OPLUS health information procfs interface"
	depends on PROC_FS
	help
	  Provide the small /proc/oplus_healthinfo interface expected by
	  OPLUS/ColorOS userspace.  It exposes the current number of system-wide
	  I/O waiters and a writable alias for vm.swappiness.

	  This is intentionally limited to the two documented proc nodes and does
	  not implement any device-specific health monitoring.

	  If built as a module, it is called oplus_healthinfo.
